        heading: "Decision Translation Under Air Composition, Pressure, And Density Basics",
        explainLikeCoach: "Translation means converting physics to one sentence a coach can act on. Example: if pregame density is in the bottom quartile of this park's history, outfield depth and pitch-plan risk tolerance may both need adjustment. Pair every recommendation with confidence and a trigger, such as: update if observed carry exceeds expected by two standard checks by inning 3. Put an inline policy marker in notes [[INLINE_DIAGRAM: forecast-to-action decision gate]]. Then publish the shared operations card [[DIAGRAM: decision tree with thresholds, owner, and reassessment trigger]].",
        formalNote: "Define a policy function $\\pi(a \\mid c_t)$ under constraints $g(a) \\le 0$ (roster, health, and tactical limits). A practical threshold rule is to intervene when $P(\\Delta y > \\tau \\mid c_t) > \\alpha$, where $\\tau$ is a carry-impact threshold and $\\alpha$ is a confidence cutoff chosen by staff. Log $(c_t, a_t, \\hat{u}_t)$ where $\\hat{u}_t$ is communicated uncertainty so postgame calibration can test both forecast skill and decision discipline. Include [[INLINE_DIAGRAM: probability threshold rule]] and [[DIAGRAM: policy table mapping atmospheric bins to tactical actions]].",
